WEBVTT

00:00:44.294 --> 00:00:46.421
The future:

00:00:46.504 --> 00:00:48.882
The polar ice caps
have melted,

00:00:48.965 --> 00:00:51.676
covering the Earth
with water.

00:00:51.760 --> 00:00:56.181
Those who survived
have adapted...

00:00:56.222 --> 00:00:58.183
to a new world.

00:05:26.991 --> 00:05:30.327
Bad luck, English.

00:05:30.369 --> 00:05:34.957
But the Slavers are producing
a good grade of poxy these days.

00:05:34.999 --> 00:05:37.877
Cost you a handful of dirt--
or maybe that wind chime.

00:05:37.960 --> 00:05:41.714
- What are you doin’ here?
- Just waiting.

00:05:41.797 --> 00:05:44.842
Take your hand
off the sail.

00:05:44.883 --> 00:05:47.344
Take it off!

00:05:47.428 --> 00:05:51.306
I’ve seen your boat before.
Haven’t seen you.

00:05:52.349 --> 00:05:55.102
Took it legal.

00:05:55.185 --> 00:05:58.063
Previous owner was dead on the tiller
when I found it.

00:05:58.147 --> 00:06:01.066
You had another hour
before I traded up again.

00:06:01.150 --> 00:06:03.735
Just improving my means.

00:06:05.237 --> 00:06:07.573
- Well, I owe you then.
- No, thanks.

00:06:07.656 --> 00:06:12.870
I got all the supplies I need.
Just came from an atoll.

00:06:12.911 --> 00:06:15.914
Eight days east,
if you’re interested.

00:06:18.083 --> 00:06:21.753
- Two drifters meet,
something needs to be exchanged.
- I know the code.

00:06:21.837 --> 00:06:24.464
But I'll give you this one
for free.

00:06:26.049 --> 00:06:27.968
Nothing’s free
in Waterworld.

00:06:28.051 --> 00:06:29.636
Ha-ha. Yeah.

00:06:40.939 --> 00:06:43.233
Smokers.

00:06:43.275 --> 00:06:45.318
Just enough wind
to get away clean.

00:06:49.239 --> 00:06:51.241
Forget the bag.

00:06:55.245 --> 00:06:59.082
It’s not worth it. You’ll never
make it with your sails down.

00:06:59.165 --> 00:07:01.668
Hey!

00:07:13.555 --> 00:07:15.765
What can I say?

00:07:35.910 --> 00:07:39.247
- Joe, he’s goin’ for it.
- What the hell?

00:07:44.293 --> 00:07:46.337
Never seen that before.

00:07:50.133 --> 00:07:52.427
Here we go! Go!
Drive! Drive!

00:07:57.557 --> 00:08:00.518
Faster! Faster! Whoo!

00:08:21.372 --> 00:08:23.666
Come on! He’s gonna get it!
He’s gonna get it!

00:08:43.352 --> 00:08:45.604
- Pick her up!
- Get it! Get it!

00:09:14.550 --> 00:09:17.135
Oh, no!

00:10:03.431 --> 00:10:06.309
Inbound!
Straight out from the gates.

00:10:15.777 --> 00:10:17.737
English.

00:10:20.407 --> 00:10:24.452
Flag’s down, drifter.
We got enough traders.

00:10:38.132 --> 00:10:40.802
Dirt.

00:10:40.843 --> 00:10:42.804
Open the gates!

00:11:24.679 --> 00:11:27.515
Bones to berries.

00:11:27.598 --> 00:11:29.683
Veins to vine.

00:11:29.767 --> 00:11:33.979
These tendons to trees.
This blood to brine.

00:11:34.021 --> 00:11:35.689
Too old she was.

00:11:35.773 --> 00:11:40.361
This woman does leave us,
recycled and enshrined...

00:11:40.402 --> 00:11:43.280
in the presence
of Him who leads us.

00:12:01.382 --> 00:12:05.886
- What is that?

00:12:10.391 --> 00:12:12.768
You know me?

00:12:12.851 --> 00:12:14.770
I know what you are.

00:12:14.853 --> 00:12:18.649
Good. Then you know if you
look for trouble while you’re here,

00:12:18.732 --> 00:12:20.776
you’ll find more
than you can handle.

00:12:22.069 --> 00:12:24.655
You got two hours.

00:12:27.241 --> 00:12:29.201
I’ll only need one.

00:12:39.336 --> 00:12:41.880
He’s comin’ over here.

00:12:47.302 --> 00:12:49.262
- Me.
- You each get one...

00:12:49.304 --> 00:12:51.848
if everything’s here
when I get back.

00:13:00.649 --> 00:13:02.526
- Pure dirt.
-

00:13:02.609 --> 00:13:04.986
3.2 kilos.

00:13:06.988 --> 00:13:10.200
How’d you come by
so much of it?

00:13:10.283 --> 00:13:13.036
Another atoll
30 horizons west of here.

00:13:13.119 --> 00:13:15.246
Where’d they get it?

00:13:15.288 --> 00:13:18.541
- They didn’t say.
- We heard about that place--

00:13:18.625 --> 00:13:21.169
that they was all killed.

00:13:22.962 --> 00:13:25.173
- That’s why they didn’t say.
- Smokers?

00:13:25.256 --> 00:13:28.468
Maybe Smokers,
maybe Slavers.

00:13:29.886 --> 00:13:32.722
So what’s the word?
We tradin’ or not?

00:13:32.806 --> 00:13:37.519
We’ll tally it
like, uh, pure hydro.

00:13:41.105 --> 00:13:44.067
Works out to... 62 chits.

00:13:46.986 --> 00:13:48.947
I want twice that.

00:13:52.742 --> 00:13:56.829
- I just want one sip of hydro!
- No, not ’til you tell me.

00:13:56.871 --> 00:14:00.124
She got inkings on her back.
I seen her.

00:14:00.166 --> 00:14:03.377
They say if you read
the marks on the child,

00:14:03.461 --> 00:14:06.923
they’ll lead ya
all the way to Dryland.

00:14:07.006 --> 00:14:10.092
- Dryland’s a myth.
- Some still believe.

00:14:10.176 --> 00:14:13.262
They say the Smokers
even got an eye out for her.

00:14:14.972 --> 00:14:18.017
Well, then, we’d better
keep it to ourselves.

00:14:41.707 --> 00:14:44.627
- Help you?
- Yeah.

00:14:44.710 --> 00:14:46.962
- Where’s the store?
- You found it.

00:14:52.718 --> 00:14:54.678
You don’t have much.

00:14:55.888 --> 00:14:58.557
You the man
with the dirt?

00:15:16.075 --> 00:15:17.618
Skoal.

00:15:21.246 --> 00:15:23.832
- One more.
- Make it two.

00:15:23.916 --> 00:15:27.669
A man this rich will buy
for a fellow outwater, I'm sure.

00:15:27.753 --> 00:15:30.088
One.

00:15:32.549 --> 00:15:36.386
That’s an interesting
pair of boots you got.

00:15:36.428 --> 00:15:38.597
- Trade?
- No.

00:15:38.680 --> 00:15:40.766
Shame.

00:15:47.481 --> 00:15:50.442
Enola.
Hey, what are you doing?

00:15:50.525 --> 00:15:54.321
- No, you can’t do that.
- I need another piece.
I want to draw some more.

00:15:54.404 --> 00:15:57.032
I’ll get it to you.
Just stay in the back.

00:15:57.115 --> 00:16:00.243
With all those chits,
you could order up a bath.

00:16:00.285 --> 00:16:02.954
- Have you ever had a freshwater bath?
- Why are you talkin’ to me?

00:16:02.996 --> 00:16:04.956
Just being friendly.

00:16:10.212 --> 00:16:12.547
- Is that a tomato plant?
- Yeah.

00:16:12.631 --> 00:16:14.799
You have a keen eye.

00:16:14.883 --> 00:16:16.968
Saw one in a picture.
How much?

00:16:23.183 --> 00:16:25.143
Half your chits.

00:16:36.654 --> 00:16:39.782
- I’ll take them too.
- Take what?

00:16:39.824 --> 00:16:42.869
- You bought everything.
- I’ll take them shelves.

00:16:45.371 --> 00:16:48.833
So, what did you see out there
in your 15 months?

00:16:48.917 --> 00:16:51.419
- Such as?
- An end to all this water.

00:16:51.502 --> 00:16:55.006
Askin’ the wrong person.

00:16:55.089 --> 00:16:57.091
- The one they buried today?
- Uh-huh?

00:16:57.175 --> 00:16:59.677
She found the only end there is.

00:17:04.849 --> 00:17:06.809
I’ve got a proposition
for you, Mariner.

00:17:08.686 --> 00:17:13.691
- I’m not staying.
- We’re not asking you to.
All we want is your seed.

00:17:14.984 --> 00:17:17.904
We can look to our own
for impregnation,

00:17:17.987 --> 00:17:23.367
but too much of that sort of thing
gets... undesirable.

00:17:23.409 --> 00:17:26.412
When she’s pregnant,
you go on your way...

00:17:26.495 --> 00:17:29.081
with all the supplies
you need.

00:17:29.165 --> 00:17:33.169
You don’t have anything.
You’re dying.

00:17:37.840 --> 00:17:41.552
No man stays out that long
and turns down a woman.

00:17:42.887 --> 00:17:47.141
- He’s hiding something.
- Maybe he’s a Smoker spy.

00:17:57.526 --> 00:18:00.821
When the elders say so,
you can leave,

00:18:00.905 --> 00:18:02.823
and not before.

00:18:21.967 --> 00:18:23.927
Gills.

00:18:24.970 --> 00:18:29.016
- Mutation!
- He’s a mutant!

00:18:29.099 --> 00:18:31.852
My hand!

00:18:47.117 --> 00:18:49.453
Throw the nets!

00:19:21.026 --> 00:19:23.945
By what right--

00:19:25.363 --> 00:19:28.241
You pay me to keep the peace.

00:19:28.325 --> 00:19:30.243
This isn’t it.

00:19:30.326 --> 00:19:33.747
- He has killed one of ours.
- He was defending himself.

00:19:33.830 --> 00:19:37.542
- He needs to be destroyed!
- Kill him. Let’s kill him.
- That may be,

00:19:37.625 --> 00:19:40.920
but not here
and not like this.

00:20:13.035 --> 00:20:14.871
What is it?

00:20:14.954 --> 00:20:16.914
Damn.

00:20:18.124 --> 00:20:21.335
It’s tied.
I can’t get it off.

00:20:24.839 --> 00:20:28.092
Open the gate.

00:20:59.373 --> 00:21:02.751
Is it a map?

00:21:02.793 --> 00:21:06.463
- You’d tell me if you knew,
wouldn’t you, Enola?
- Mm-hmm.

00:21:09.925 --> 00:21:12.845
- What are you drawing?
- I don’t know.

00:21:14.263 --> 00:21:18.726
Helen, look. Look at
the prodigal child’s latest vision.

00:21:24.440 --> 00:21:29.528
- How soon before we can leave?
- I don’t have any idea yet
where we can go.

00:21:29.611 --> 00:21:32.948
I haven’t figured out
the tattoo on her back.

00:21:32.990 --> 00:21:36.618
I’m a stupid man.
The answer’s right there.

00:21:36.702 --> 00:21:38.704
It’s just beyond me.

00:21:41.748 --> 00:21:43.834
Maybe he knows.

00:21:52.509 --> 00:21:57.014
Oh, yes, I see.
They are webbed.

00:21:57.097 --> 00:22:00.851
One, two, three, four,
five, six, seven, eight, nine,
ten digits. That’s wonderful.

00:22:00.934 --> 00:22:03.937
They tell me, too,
that you have gills.

00:22:03.979 --> 00:22:08.650
Isotropic gills. Are they merely
vestigial or are they functional now?

00:22:08.692 --> 00:22:12.237
My name is Gregor. I’ve just come
to pay you a little vi-- vi--

00:22:13.822 --> 00:22:17.075
Oh, my God.

00:22:17.158 --> 00:22:20.203
I’m sorry.
I’m not laughing at you.

00:22:20.287 --> 00:22:23.331
I’m excited. Your gills.
They’re functional.

00:22:23.415 --> 00:22:27.043
Icthyus Sapiens.
You can breathe in the water.

00:22:27.127 --> 00:22:31.006
How deep can you go?
Look, I'm only here...

00:22:31.047 --> 00:22:33.675
because I want to learn
more about you.

00:22:38.763 --> 00:22:42.142
You don’t like humans
very much, do you?

00:22:42.183 --> 00:22:45.812
I can’t say that I blame you.
But tell me:

00:22:45.854 --> 00:22:49.482
- Are all of your kind as
bad-tempered as you are?
-

00:22:52.068 --> 00:22:54.529
- I have no ’’kind.’’
- Oh, fish rot.

00:22:54.612 --> 00:22:58.032
I’d be surprised if there
weren’t others, and if there aren’t,

00:22:58.074 --> 00:23:01.494
there will be eventually.

00:23:01.536 --> 00:23:04.872
Anyway, I've come here
because I need to ask you a question.

00:23:04.956 --> 00:23:08.876
Where-- Where did
your dirt come from?

00:23:08.960 --> 00:23:11.379
Is it from Dryland?

00:23:11.421 --> 00:23:13.548
Do you know what this is?

00:23:15.508 --> 00:23:17.885
The ancients-- They did something
terrible, didn’t they?

00:23:17.969 --> 00:23:21.722
To cause all this water.
Hundreds-- Hundreds of years ago.

00:23:21.806 --> 00:23:24.851
If I tell you,
will you open this lock?

00:23:27.353 --> 00:23:30.231
I haven’t a key.

00:23:30.273 --> 00:23:33.025
- There’s a mooring cleat down there.
- What?

00:23:33.067 --> 00:23:36.153
- Good as any key.
- A mooring cleat?

00:23:38.239 --> 00:23:40.992
I won’t hurt anyone.
I’ll just leave.

00:23:42.326 --> 00:23:45.621
- I’ll be right back.
- Gregor!

00:23:45.705 --> 00:23:47.665
What’s your business there?

00:23:47.748 --> 00:23:49.875
- Move along!
- I’m not a brave man.

00:23:49.917 --> 00:23:54.255
If you know anything about Dryland,
please tell me. Please!

00:23:55.589 --> 00:23:57.508
Don’t let it die with you.

00:23:57.591 --> 00:24:00.302
No, no, no, no.
Stop!

00:24:00.386 --> 00:24:04.056
Gregor! Move along!

00:24:38.924 --> 00:24:44.137
After considerable deliberation
of the evidence at hand,

00:24:44.179 --> 00:24:47.641
it is our decision
that this mute-o...

00:24:47.724 --> 00:24:50.978
does, indeed,
constitute a threat.

00:24:51.019 --> 00:24:53.981
Therefore, in the interest
of public safety,

00:24:54.064 --> 00:24:57.609
he is hereby sentenced
to be recycled...

00:24:57.651 --> 00:25:00.529
in the customary fashion.

00:25:00.612 --> 00:25:02.489
Proceed.

00:25:08.412 --> 00:25:11.248
I’m sorry.

00:25:15.043 --> 00:25:17.170
Bones to berries.

00:25:17.212 --> 00:25:19.840
Veins to vines.

00:25:19.881 --> 00:25:23.677
His tendons to trees.
His blood to brine.

00:25:23.718 --> 00:25:26.846
Too strange for life he was.

00:25:26.888 --> 00:25:31.351
This mute-o now does leave us,

00:25:31.434 --> 00:25:34.271
recycled and entombed,

00:25:34.688 --> 00:25:37.565
in the presence
of Him who leads us.

00:25:47.534 --> 00:25:52.247
Smokers!
Dead out of the sun!

00:25:55.416 --> 00:25:58.878
To your posts!

00:26:13.559 --> 00:26:16.479
Oh, my God! Oh, my God!

00:26:26.823 --> 00:26:29.575
- Kill!
- There!

00:26:39.585 --> 00:26:42.421
We are safe
behind these walls.

00:26:43.923 --> 00:26:45.883
- Aren’t we?
-

00:26:51.722 --> 00:26:54.809
- Let me out!

00:26:56.477 --> 00:26:58.813
Let me out!
I’ll fight!

00:27:28.258 --> 00:27:30.177
Give me the key
to the city now.

00:27:34.014 --> 00:27:36.350
Let’s go!
Let’s go! Let’s go!

00:27:39.019 --> 00:27:41.939
Floor it!
Floor it! Floor it!

00:28:03.168 --> 00:28:05.504
Swab it! Swab it!

00:28:05.587 --> 00:28:09.257
Goddamn! More ammo!

00:28:23.647 --> 00:28:25.690
Break down the door!

00:28:29.486 --> 00:28:32.572
- My God!
-

00:28:32.656 --> 00:28:35.033
Ha!

00:28:37.244 --> 00:28:40.246
We’ll have this atoll
in no time.

00:28:43.541 --> 00:28:45.502
Crank it!
Crank it!

00:28:49.547 --> 00:28:51.800
Look!

00:29:10.485 --> 00:29:12.695
Look out!

00:29:35.218 --> 00:29:37.136
Oh, no!

00:29:48.064 --> 00:29:50.858
You get that goin’!
Fill ’em up!

00:30:28.812 --> 00:30:32.149
- Helen, come quickly!

00:30:32.232 --> 00:30:34.401
Helen!

00:31:02.387 --> 00:31:05.849
You’re not supposed to go yet!

00:31:05.891 --> 00:31:08.268
Infernal machine!

00:31:11.772 --> 00:31:14.524
Gregor. Gregor, wait!

00:31:14.608 --> 00:31:17.944
Helen, I tried. There was an accident.
I can’t make it stop. Hurry!

00:31:18.028 --> 00:31:21.448
You can make it if you try. Run!
Up those stairs. Run! Quickly!

00:31:21.531 --> 00:31:25.744
- Wait! Wait!
- I’ll throw you a rope. Run quickly!

00:31:25.827 --> 00:31:28.830
- Throw the rope now. Run, Enola.
- Slow down! Wait!

00:31:28.872 --> 00:31:32.834
- Throw the rope. No! No!
- Wait!

00:31:34.377 --> 00:31:36.546
- Gregor, don’t leave us!
- Oh, no!

00:31:36.630 --> 00:31:38.882
I’m sorry!
It was an accident!

00:31:43.261 --> 00:31:47.015
Helen! Enola!
Helen, I'm sorry!

00:31:56.024 --> 00:31:59.402
Shoot him.
Shoot him.

00:32:26.179 --> 00:32:29.640
If I let you out of here,
you’re taking us with you.

00:32:30.933 --> 00:32:32.935
Sure.

00:32:34.604 --> 00:32:36.856
Enola, get down.

00:32:38.524 --> 00:32:40.735
Here. Get over here.
Get down.

00:32:40.777 --> 00:32:42.737
Hurry!
Come on!

00:32:45.698 --> 00:32:48.034
Get the gate.

00:33:20.733 --> 00:33:22.651
Run!

00:33:47.009 --> 00:33:48.927
Hurry up!

00:33:49.011 --> 00:33:50.888
Kamikazes. Come on!

00:34:19.583 --> 00:34:21.585
That made a hole.

00:34:33.221 --> 00:34:36.725
Find her!
Get the girl!

00:34:41.813 --> 00:34:43.899
There!

00:34:50.864 --> 00:34:54.159
Go get that guy!
Go! Kill him!

00:34:58.246 --> 00:35:00.665
- Wow!
- Enola!

00:35:11.092 --> 00:35:14.137
- You’re too slow!
- Run to the other side.

00:35:16.014 --> 00:35:19.142
- Come on!

00:35:22.353 --> 00:35:26.441
- Grab on! Hold on, hold on.

00:35:30.486 --> 00:35:32.530
I’m stuck!
I can’t make it through!

00:35:32.613 --> 00:35:35.366
- Let her go!
-

00:35:36.451 --> 00:35:38.369
Just drop her!

00:35:53.176 --> 00:35:56.971
Turn the wheel.
The wheel! Turn it!

00:35:59.932 --> 00:36:02.893
That! Come on! Push it!

00:36:02.977 --> 00:36:05.646
- I am!
- Hurry! Now pull!

00:36:05.688 --> 00:36:09.608
Push it! Push it hard!
Push it hard!

00:36:09.650 --> 00:36:12.695
Okay, okay! Now pull this!
Pull this!

00:36:12.778 --> 00:36:16.240
Pull! Pull it!
Hurry!

00:36:26.417 --> 00:36:29.670
- Enola, jump.

00:36:32.006 --> 00:36:34.425
- Look at me. Jump! Now!
- Okay!

00:36:51.191 --> 00:36:56.029
Well, excuse me! Did I say anybody
could leave before the battle was over?

00:36:56.113 --> 00:36:58.031
- Did I?
- No! No!

00:36:58.115 --> 00:37:00.534
Well, do somethin’.
I hate sails.

00:37:09.835 --> 00:37:13.046
Hey! Can you steer?

00:37:13.130 --> 00:37:15.048
Can I trust you?

00:37:49.583 --> 00:37:53.169
Answer me this, somebody.
Why is that boat still firin’?

00:37:54.254 --> 00:37:56.923
- What’s that cousin’s name?
- Chuck.

00:37:56.965 --> 00:38:01.177
- Hey, Chuck!
-
He’s pulling him right into us.

00:38:01.261 --> 00:38:05.640
Maybe he doesn’t answer to ’’Chuck.’’
Call him ’’Charles.’’ Charles!

00:38:06.766 --> 00:38:10.812
Stop him! Stop him!

00:38:18.319 --> 00:38:20.321
Charles!

00:38:22.156 --> 00:38:24.117
Adios, cousins.

00:39:09.996 --> 00:39:12.164
She’s here somewhere.
Keep lookin’.

00:39:12.248 --> 00:39:14.834
Stop it!

00:39:24.260 --> 00:39:29.849
- What you got?
- Couple of heartbeats over there.
Aren’t sayin’ much.

00:39:29.932 --> 00:39:34.019
If you’ll notice the arterial
nature of the blood comin’
from the hole in my head,

00:39:34.061 --> 00:39:38.399
you can assume that we’re
all havin’ a real lousy day.

00:39:38.482 --> 00:39:42.319
So here it is: I need to know
about that tattooed girl.

00:39:43.862 --> 00:39:46.198
First one that
tells me lives.

00:39:46.240 --> 00:39:51.036
- I saw a girl. I saw, I saw--
- It was-- Sh-She had
a big tattoo on her.

00:39:53.330 --> 00:39:56.208
You won.
Start over.

00:39:56.291 --> 00:39:58.419
I saw a girl.
I’m not sure,

00:39:58.502 --> 00:40:03.465
but I think she got on that boat
with three hulls.

00:40:03.549 --> 00:40:07.886
- The boat that cost me
a thousand G’s of go-juice?
- Yeah, the mute-o’s boat.

00:40:07.970 --> 00:40:11.890
- Mute-o?
- Yeah. He got these slits here.

00:40:11.932 --> 00:40:15.310
Like--
Like fish gills.

00:40:15.394 --> 00:40:17.646
He wasn’t really a man.

00:40:17.729 --> 00:40:20.399
A fluke of evolution.

00:40:21.942 --> 00:40:24.319
Oh, I'm sorry.
A fluke of, uh--

00:40:24.403 --> 00:40:26.780
- Evolution.
- I know!

00:40:26.863 --> 00:40:30.742
- No! No, you said
you wouldn’t kill me!
- Did I say that?

00:40:30.784 --> 00:40:33.912
- Witnesses, anybody, did I?
- Yes, yes, yes! You said--

00:40:33.995 --> 00:40:36.540
- You said it.
- Oh, I may have.

00:40:38.583 --> 00:40:40.502
I may have.

00:40:47.050 --> 00:40:49.302
We get to the ’Deez,

00:40:50.595 --> 00:40:53.890
tank up that sky boat;
send it out on patrol.

00:40:55.141 --> 00:40:57.852
We gotta keep an eye out...

00:40:57.936 --> 00:41:00.313
for that ichthy-freak.

00:41:24.087 --> 00:41:26.130
You been there, haven’t you?

00:41:30.969 --> 00:41:33.555
Dryland?

00:41:33.638 --> 00:41:35.807
You know where it is.

00:41:36.766 --> 00:41:38.768
Yeah, I know where it is.

00:41:41.854 --> 00:41:44.524
And, uh-- And we’re going?

00:41:45.650 --> 00:41:47.610
You and I are.

00:41:49.153 --> 00:41:52.323
The kid we gotta pitch
over the side.

00:41:54.158 --> 00:41:58.162
- What?
- My boat’s tore up.

00:41:58.246 --> 00:42:00.748
I’m takin’ on water.

00:42:00.832 --> 00:42:04.252
I’d be lucky to get
half a hydro ration out of that.

00:42:04.335 --> 00:42:07.964
You know--
I said I won’t drink.

00:42:08.005 --> 00:42:10.591
For 12 days?

00:42:12.176 --> 00:42:15.096
No. It’s better
one of you dies now...

00:42:15.179 --> 00:42:17.223
than both of you die slow.

00:42:17.306 --> 00:42:19.517
Wait. Wait.

00:42:19.558 --> 00:42:22.019
We saved your life.
We got you out.

00:42:22.103 --> 00:42:26.190
No, you got me out so you
could get out. We’re even.

00:42:26.273 --> 00:42:28.317
She can cook.
She can fish.

00:42:28.359 --> 00:42:30.653
- So can I.
- Then take my necklace.
Take my necklace.

00:42:30.694 --> 00:42:32.988
- I got better ones below.
- No, look!

00:42:33.030 --> 00:42:35.866
Oh.

00:42:35.950 --> 00:42:39.036
After what you went through
back there on the atoll,

00:42:39.119 --> 00:42:42.289
I can understand
why you would want to.

00:42:42.373 --> 00:42:44.375
But she’s a child.

00:42:55.386 --> 00:42:57.805
Is there something else then?

00:43:03.227 --> 00:43:05.813
Enola! Go below.

00:43:06.939 --> 00:43:08.899
Enola.

00:43:19.243 --> 00:43:22.579
Yeah. You said so yourself.

00:43:24.456 --> 00:43:27.209
Been out there a long time.

00:44:12.879 --> 00:44:15.924
Couple hours ago,
I was potential dirt to you.

00:44:15.965 --> 00:44:19.386
- We’re not like that.
- You all are.

00:44:24.974 --> 00:44:28.269
Know what I was really thinkin’?

00:44:28.311 --> 00:44:31.481
Why I don’t drop both of you
in my wake right now.

00:44:32.815 --> 00:44:35.360
You got nothin’ I need.

00:44:51.292 --> 00:44:53.669
You’re taking us to Dryland.

00:44:58.007 --> 00:45:00.843
Killing’s a hard thing to do well.

00:45:00.885 --> 00:45:04.347
- Believe me. I’m not
the one to start on.
- Both of us!

00:45:09.852 --> 00:45:12.438
How long you plan
to hold that on me?

00:45:12.522 --> 00:45:14.690
As long as it takes.

00:45:17.235 --> 00:45:20.279
- Okay.
- No!

00:45:21.948 --> 00:45:25.076
Let me out of here!

00:45:25.159 --> 00:45:28.996
Where the hell are you?
Don’t you touch my child.

00:45:29.038 --> 00:45:30.998
Come here!

00:46:19.213 --> 00:46:21.924
Okay, now don’t move, okay?
There.

00:46:22.007 --> 00:46:25.427
Ohh. Oh, lookin’
real good, yeah.

00:46:25.469 --> 00:46:27.804
There. There.

00:46:27.888 --> 00:46:29.806
All done.

00:46:29.890 --> 00:46:32.893
Now, there may be some small problem
in depth perception.

00:46:32.935 --> 00:46:35.812
Well, it better not
screw up my short game.

00:46:38.273 --> 00:46:40.692
- Well?
- Looks good.
I like it. Yeah.

00:46:40.776 --> 00:46:43.862
- I like it better than your real eye.
- Much better.

00:46:43.945 --> 00:46:47.449
- What do you say, Toby? The truth.
- Looks like shit.

00:46:47.532 --> 00:46:50.452
That’s why I love children.
No guile.

00:46:54.748 --> 00:46:58.210
It does look like shit.

00:46:58.293 --> 00:47:00.212
And it feels like cold shit!

00:47:00.295 --> 00:47:02.797
Deacon? What--

00:47:04.174 --> 00:47:07.302
I’m sorry. I-lt’s just that
there’s a problem in the pit.

00:47:07.344 --> 00:47:09.304
Maybe you should come.

00:47:14.809 --> 00:47:18.146
- Let’s drive.
-

00:47:23.818 --> 00:47:27.489
The pit. Don’t bother
with the scenic route.

00:47:27.530 --> 00:47:29.491
Drive!

00:47:30.617 --> 00:47:32.827
Hey, it’s drivin’ better.

00:47:44.797 --> 00:47:47.050
Get off!

00:47:48.134 --> 00:47:50.511
Get over there.
Get out of the way.

00:47:50.595 --> 00:47:52.722
All right, all right, all right.
Okay, okay.

00:47:55.975 --> 00:47:59.395
You guys are great.
Bless all you cousins over there.

00:47:59.479 --> 00:48:03.941
Keep up the good work.
Growth is progress. Growth is progress.

00:48:04.025 --> 00:48:08.696
Somebody!
Hey, up there!

00:48:08.738 --> 00:48:10.698
Take it off!

00:48:13.159 --> 00:48:16.496
- Yes.
- Your Deaconship.

00:48:16.537 --> 00:48:20.499
Hello. Good morning.
Or night,

00:48:20.541 --> 00:48:23.085
whichever the case may be.

00:48:23.169 --> 00:48:26.047
- What is it? I’m a busy man.
- I thought you should know.

00:48:26.088 --> 00:48:28.758
We’re down to exactly...

00:48:28.841 --> 00:48:32.845
four feet, nine inches
of black stuff.

00:48:34.430 --> 00:48:39.101
- Thank you, sir.

00:48:39.185 --> 00:48:42.063
- How many G’s is that after refinin’?
- Maybe three refuelers.

00:48:42.104 --> 00:48:45.733
- We’ll burn through that in two lunars.
- Sweet Joe!

00:48:45.775 --> 00:48:49.403
Will somebody please tell me
what’s happened to this place?

00:48:49.445 --> 00:48:51.530
We outgrowed it.

00:48:51.572 --> 00:48:55.451
All right, the only thing
that is important is the tattooed girl.

00:48:55.534 --> 00:48:58.913
We don’t spare any go-juice
findin’ her.

00:48:58.996 --> 00:49:02.082
We don’t waste it anywhere else.
You cancel all those tractor pulls...

00:49:02.166 --> 00:49:04.043
and all that stuff
until later.

00:49:04.084 --> 00:49:06.086
You got it?

00:49:07.588 --> 00:49:10.424
Dryland is the mother lode.

00:49:10.507 --> 00:49:12.634
On your toes.

00:49:14.094 --> 00:49:16.013
Excellent.

00:49:45.500 --> 00:49:48.795
- Hi.
- Move.

00:49:48.879 --> 00:49:51.256
Enola!
Enola, come here!

00:49:53.550 --> 00:49:55.469
Come on!

00:49:57.471 --> 00:49:59.431
Enola, come over here.

00:50:12.986 --> 00:50:14.738
Hey!

00:50:16.990 --> 00:50:21.536
- What are ya doin’?
- Decorating your boat. It’s ugly.

00:50:25.665 --> 00:50:28.835
- Where did you get this?
- From down below.

00:50:28.877 --> 00:50:31.588
This is mine!
You don’t touch anything of mine.

00:50:31.671 --> 00:50:35.049
- I drew it for you.
- You don’t draw on anything.
You understand?

00:50:40.638 --> 00:50:42.557
What--

00:50:44.809 --> 00:50:47.770
This is my boat.
I got it the way I like it.

00:50:47.854 --> 00:50:50.648
You take up space
and you slow me down.

00:50:54.569 --> 00:50:57.196
You know, she’s just a little girl.

00:50:57.280 --> 00:51:00.408
- She doesn’t know your rules.
- You wanna stay?

00:51:00.491 --> 00:51:02.410
You teach her.

00:51:21.888 --> 00:51:24.056
Enola, what’d I tell you?

00:51:29.353 --> 00:51:31.731
You’re not so tough.
You know that?

00:51:36.068 --> 00:51:37.987
How many people
have you killed?

00:51:40.781 --> 00:51:43.659
Ten? Twenty?

00:51:45.619 --> 00:51:50.249
- You talk a lot.
- I talk a lot ’cause
you don’t talk at all.

00:51:50.291 --> 00:51:52.251
Now how many?

00:51:54.086 --> 00:51:57.798
- Including little girls?
- I’m not afraid of you.

00:52:01.677 --> 00:52:04.930
I told Helen you wouldn’t be so ugly
if you cut your hair.

00:52:08.309 --> 00:52:10.936
In fact, you talk all the time.

00:52:11.020 --> 00:52:13.105
- It’s like a storm
when you’re around.
- Enola!

00:52:13.188 --> 00:52:15.774
Hey! What are you doing?

00:52:15.858 --> 00:52:18.986
- Helen!
- You bastard!
She can’t swim!

00:52:19.069 --> 00:52:21.947
Help me! Helen!

00:52:23.615 --> 00:52:25.576
Helen, help me!

00:52:25.617 --> 00:52:28.245
Helen!

00:52:28.287 --> 00:52:30.330
Helen, help me!

00:52:38.839 --> 00:52:41.508
Helen! Helen!

00:52:41.592 --> 00:52:44.136
Hold on!

00:52:44.177 --> 00:52:46.597
Look at me.
Look at me. Look at me.

00:52:47.681 --> 00:52:51.685
Oh, please, come back.
Please!

00:52:51.768 --> 00:52:55.272
Please! Oh, please!

00:53:00.068 --> 00:53:02.654
Hey!

00:53:04.239 --> 00:53:06.616
Hold on.
Okay, almost...

00:53:08.160 --> 00:53:10.120
there.

00:53:20.171 --> 00:53:21.423
Thanks. I swear,

00:53:22.716 --> 00:53:25.302
if you ever touch her again--

00:53:25.343 --> 00:53:27.512
You son of a bitch.
Look at me.

00:53:27.554 --> 00:53:30.140
You will go to bed that night,
and you will never wake up.

00:53:30.181 --> 00:53:32.517
- Shut up.
- What?

00:53:32.559 --> 00:53:35.520
- Smokers?
- Yeah.

00:53:35.603 --> 00:53:37.856
Can’t we outrun them?

00:53:37.939 --> 00:53:41.901
- Not with my sail down.

00:54:00.044 --> 00:54:04.090
- What are you thinkin’ about?
- That’s a nice touch.

00:54:04.173 --> 00:54:06.092
That’s them.

00:54:12.265 --> 00:54:15.143
Don’t hit the kid.

00:54:29.574 --> 00:54:32.451
Hey!

00:54:37.415 --> 00:54:39.500
Coward!

00:54:47.717 --> 00:54:50.052
Fuck!

00:55:17.496 --> 00:55:20.290
No!

00:55:41.144 --> 00:55:43.063
Cut it!

00:55:51.405 --> 00:55:54.157
Come on! Come on!

00:56:25.897 --> 00:56:29.150
All right. Okay.

00:57:29.085 --> 00:57:32.338
Oh, I'm really sorry.

00:57:32.421 --> 00:57:35.591
I’m sorry.
But you didn’t give me much choice.

00:57:35.633 --> 00:57:38.594
Oh, I know.

00:57:38.678 --> 00:57:41.430
But you ran away.
I-- What?

00:57:41.472 --> 00:57:45.309
What are you do--
No! Please, no! No!

00:57:54.402 --> 00:57:58.697
Don’t ever touch
anything on my boat again.

00:58:02.118 --> 00:58:04.120
She said she was sorry!

00:58:08.123 --> 00:58:10.918
That means you’re supposed
to say something back!

00:58:34.149 --> 00:58:36.151
- Did you say somethin’?
- Mm-mmm.

